.TH nino 1 "November 2026" "Version 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nino \- CECP/WinBoard chess engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nino
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBNino\fR is a chess engine written in C, originally created as a university programming project. It partially implements the Chess Engine Communication Protocol (CECP) and has been tested with XBoard, WinBoard, and Arena.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h
Display a short help text.
.TP
.B \-v
Display engine version information.
.TP
.B \-tt \fIsize\fR
Set the amount of memory (in bytes) to assign to the transposition table. If zero, the transposition table is turned off.
.TP
.B \-pt \fIsize\fR
Set the amount of memory (in bytes) to assign to the pawn table. If zero, no pawn table is used.
.TP
.B \-book \fIfile\fR
Use \fIfile\fR as the opening book.
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
When running \fBnino\fR interactively in a terminal, the following commands are available:
.TP
.B = \fIor\fR set
Set the board to the initial state.
.TP
.B / \fIor\fR boardinfo
Print the current state of the board and other information.
.TP
.B \fIxxxx\fR
An algebraic notation chess move (e.g., e2e4). Makes that move on the board.
.TP
.B ; n \fIor\fR play n \fIor\fR search n
Start the chess engine to find a move using a max ply of n.
.TP
.B \e n \fIor\fR think n
Start the chess engine to run for n seconds reaching the maximum ply possible (default is 5 seconds).
.TP
.B \- \fIor\fR undo
Undo the last move.
.TP
.B fen
Print the FEN notation string for the current position.
.TP
.B clear
Clear the terminal screen.
.TP
.B debug
Toggle debug mode on/off.
.TP
.B perft n
Run a performance test with an n-ply depth.
.TP
.B epdtest \fIfile\fR
Read an EPD file and perform a performance test.
.TP
.B eval
Evaluate the current position and output the result.
.TP
.B h \fIor\fR hash
Output the hash for the current position.
.TP
.B see \fIsq\fR
Evaluate Static Exchange Evaluation (SEE) for the specified square (0-63).
.TP
.B , \fIor\fR moves
Show all available moves.
.TP
.B < \fIor\fR captures
Generate and output all captures.
.TP
.B attacked
Print a board representation with all attacked squares.
.TP
.B +escape
Generate and output moves that escape from check.
.TP
.B order
Order available moves based on heuristics and output them.
.TP
.B exit, bye \fIor\fR quit
Exit the program.
